\fs48 \cf2 Floating-point numbers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Mojo provides several floating-point types for representing real numbers at different precisions. Since floating-point values use a fixed number of bits, some numbers can't be represented exactly.\
The floating-point types 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float64
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float32
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 Float16
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  follow the IEEE 754-2008 standard for representing floating-point values. Each type includes a sign bit, a set of bits representing an exponent, and a set of bits representing the mantissa (also called fraction or significand). Table 3 shows how these types are represented in memory.\
